# Append-log files merge with git's built-in union driver: a conflict keeps BOTH
# sides' additions instead of blocking. SESSION and BACKLOG are logs by design —
# parallel PRs append entries / flip task checkboxes in the same spots constantly,
# and every collision is "both sides are real data, keep both."
# Cost is cosmetic only (adjacent entries may land in odd order) — tidy in the next commit.
#
# ai/MEMORY.md is deliberately EXCLUDED: decision entries get *edited* (superseded →
# stub), and union would silently interleave two edits of the same lines with no
# conflict marker. MEMORY conflicts stop for the project owner (see ai/TEAM.md
# working agreements) — never auto-merge the decision ledger.
ai/SESSION.md merge=union
ai/BACKLOG.md merge=union
